:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=CHKPRDOPT.Check Product Option (CHKPRDOPT)
:P.Use the Check Product Option (CHKPRDOPT) command to check that a
product's objects are all there.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKPRDOPT/PRDID'.Product ID (PRDID)
:P.A product identifier&colon. seven characters, QS00SS1 for example.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKPRDOPT/RLS'.Release (RLS)
:P.A release, in the form VxRyMz.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKPRDOPT/OPTION'.Product option (OPTION)
:P.The product option for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*BASE:EPK.
:PD.The base pool.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKPRDOPT/DETAIL'.Detail (DETAIL)
:P.The detail for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:PT.:PK.*FULL:EPK.
:PD.Full.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTLICPGM.Delete Licensed Program (DLTLICPGM)
:P.Use the Delete Licensed Program (DLTLICPGM) command to delete a
licensed program or one of its options.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTLICPGM/LICPGM'.Product (LICPGM)
:P.A licensed program by its seven-character product identifier, QS00SS1
for example.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTLICPGM/OPTION'.Optional part to be deleted (OPTION)
:P.The optional part to be deleted for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*BASE:EPK.
:PD.The base pool.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTLICPGM/RLS'.Release (RLS)
:P.A release, in the form VxRyMz.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTLICPGM/LNG'.Language for licensed program (LNG)
:P.The language feature of the licensed program.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=INSLNG.Install Language (INSLNG)
:P.Use the Install Language (INSLNG) command to install a secondary
language&colon. the language library QSYS followed by the feature code,
holding the language's message files and its sign-on display files. Put
the library ahead of QSYS in the system part of the library list to see
its text; a job whose language identifier is the library's language gets
it there at its start and on CHGJOB LANGID. In this release the only
secondary language shipped is Spanish (2931), a scaffold whose message
files carry machine-translated first-level text only.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INSLNG/LNG'.Language feature (LNG)
:P.The feature code of the language to install, such as 2931 for
Spanish. The library made is QSYS followed by the code.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INSLNG/REPLACE'.Replace objects (REPLACE)
:P.Whether the language's objects that are already in its library are
replaced with the ones the system carries. Objects missing from the
library are always created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSLICPGM.Licensed Program Panel (QSLICPGM)
:P.Use the Licensed Program Panel (QSLICPGM) command to one GO LICPGM
panel (Quartz's; the menu's options).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSLICPGM/OPTION'.GO LICPGM option (OPTION)
:P.The GO LICPGM option for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.The value must be '1', '10', '11', '12', '13', '20', '21', '22'.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSPKGPRD.Package Product from Manifest (QSPKGPRD)
:P.Use the Package Product from Manifest (QSPKGPRD) command to build a
product from a manifest stream file (Quartz's).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSPKGPRD/MANIFEST'.Manifest stream file (MANIFEST)
:P.The manifest stream file for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSPKGPRD/SAVF'.Save file for the product (SAVF)
:P.The save file, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RSTLICPGM.Restore Licensed Program (RSTLICPGM)
:P.Use the Restore Licensed Program (RSTLICPGM) command to install a
licensed program from media or a save file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLICPGM/LICPGM'.Product (LICPGM)
:P.A licensed program by its seven-character product identifier, QS00SS1
for example.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLICPGM/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SAVF:EPK.
:PD.A save file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLICPGM/OPTION'.Optional part to be restored (OPTION)
:P.The optional part to be restored for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BASE:EPK.
:PD.The base pool.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLICPGM/RSTOBJ'.Type of object to be restored (RSTOBJ)
:P.The type of object to be restored for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*PGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the program.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LNG.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLICPGM/LNG'.Language for licensed program (LNG)
:P.The language feature of the licensed program.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PRIMARY.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLICPGM/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLICPGM/REPLACERLS'.Release to be replaced (REPLACERLS)
:P.The release to be replaced for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLICPGM/RLS'.Release (RLS)
:P.A release, in the form VxRyMz.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLICPGM/ENDOPT'.End of media option (ENDOPT)
:P.What the device does with the tape when the operation ends&colon.
leave it where it is, rewind it, or rewind and unload it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound.
:PT.:PK.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is; the next operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLICPGM/SAVF'.Save file (SAVF)
:P.The save file, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SAVLICPGM.Save Licensed Program (SAVLICPGM)
:P.Use the Save Licensed Program (SAVLICPGM) command to save a licensed
program for installing elsewhere.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLICPGM/LICPGM'.Product (LICPGM)
:P.A licensed program by its seven-character product identifier, QS00SS1
for example.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLICPGM/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SAVF:EPK.
:PD.A save file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLICPGM/OPTION'.Optional part to be saved (OPTION)
:P.The optional part to be saved for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BASE:EPK.
:PD.The base pool.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 5 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLICPGM/OBJTYPE'.Object type (OBJTYPE)
:P.The type or types of the objects the command works on.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*PGM:EPK.
:PD.The value of the program.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LNG.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLICPGM/LNG'.Language for licensed program (LNG)
:P.The language feature of the licensed program.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLICPGM/RLS'.Release (RLS)
:P.A release, in the form VxRyMz.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.The only one&colon. an error is sent when more than one matches.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 6 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLICPGM/ENDOPT'.End of media option (ENDOPT)
:P.What the device does with the tape when the operation ends&colon.
leave it where it is, rewind it, or rewind and unload it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound.
:PT.:PK.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is; the next operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLICPGM/SAVF'.Save file (SAVF)
:P.The save file, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLICPGM/CLEAR'.Clear (CLEAR)
:P.The clear for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*AFTER:EPK.
:PD.After the reference entry.
:PT.:PK.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.What is there is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLICPGM/DTACPR'.Data compression (DTACPR)
:P.Whether the data is compressed as it is written.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*LOW:EPK.
:PD.Low.
:PT.:PK.*MEDIUM:EPK.
:PD.Medium.
:PT.:PK.*HIGH:EPK.
:PD.High.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLICPGM/TGTRLS'.Target release (TGTRLS)
:P.The release of the operating system the object is created for.
*CURRENT is this release; *PRV is the previous one.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.This release.
:PT.:PK.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKSFWAGR.Work with Software Agreements (WRKSFWAGR)
:P.Use the Work with Software Agreements (WRKSFWAGR) command to work
with the software agreements.
:P.The command has no parameters.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
